MID_SE_Dit_Led_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_001: Ah, a fine opponent! Hrah!
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_002: Hehe. You enjoyed that, I take it?
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_003: I get plenty of requests for music, but I don't often\nget requests for a Demonic Beast.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_004: To be honest, I'm not sure how to feel about it.\nI bring these creatures here...only to be slaughtered.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_005: Oh? Yet you seem pleased.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_006: Well, I usually play just to get in the good graces of\nsome scumbag.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_007: But you're no scumbag. And you have a pretty face.\nSo, I suppose it's not so bad this time.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_008: Hmm.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_009: You don't get it... I'm saying that I'm glad you're just\ninterested in my Demonic Beasts—and not me.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_010: I cultivated this power for one reason only...\nTo kill someone I loathe. To kill Bertrand.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_011: I don't care if this power comes to me from Balor.\nI will use it if it allows me to get my revenge.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_012: But now he's dead... Dead when I wanted so very\nmuch to play my song of revenge for him...
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_013: I care not for revenge—only for dueling the strong.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_014: You don't ever think about revenge? But surely\nyou've invited it from having cut down so many.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_015: Has no one ever come after you seething with rage\nand ready to avenge a loved one you killed?
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_016: I do not recall. They were beneath my notice.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_017: We may have walked the same blood-soaked road,\nbut I don't understand you.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_018: And that's fine by me. I hate people acting like they\nunderstand when they don't.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_019: Anyway, my song is perfect for a murderer's ears.\nI'll play it for you again sometime.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_B_020: She is an odd one.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_001: Hello, Dietrich. Let me guess...you want me to play\nanother Demonic Beast into existence for you?
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_002: No. I do have a question for you, though.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_003: You summon Demonic Beasts without a care, and\nsmile as I cut them down. How?
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_004: What's that supposed to mean?
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_005: Summoning these beasts is a skill that was hard-\nearned. Seeing them destroyed cannot be pleasant.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_006: I thought human feelings were "beneath your notice."\nThis sudden concern of yours is...unexpected.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_007: Besides, I told you how I feel about people acting like\nthey understand.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_008: Maybe you feel closer to me since we've now fought\ntogether, but please stop prying.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_009: I have no further need for words. It is time to fight!
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_010: Hey! What the hell do you think you're doing? How\ndare you draw your sword on me!
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_011: Aaah!
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_012: Stand, or die on the ground.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_013: Die? ME? At the tip of this bastard's blade?\nI will not!
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_014: You're the one who's going to die, Dietrich.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_015: Yes, the darkness rises... I will enjoy this!
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_016: After all that, I still couldn't kill you. Please, that\nsmug look on your face disgusts me.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_017: Killing is the only way you experience pleasure,\nisn't it? How lovely.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_018: Pleasure? Were you not pleased also? You brought\nyour skill to bear by unleashing that beast.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_019: What?! What the hell are you saying?
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_020: You diminish your talents, but they are formidable.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_021: You allowed me to slay the beasts because you take\nno pleasure in your talents.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_022: So? A song that summons a monster like that—\na monster meant only for murder...it's repulsive.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_023: I despise this power. I only use it because it's a\nmeans to an end. Nothing more.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_024: Truly? To me, life pulses through your song. It is\nthe very cry of your soul.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_025: It is no mere melody. The sound is itself you. Am\nI wrong?
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_026: Wait, did you try to kill me so you could...\nunderstand me?
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_027: Unbelievable. You have a strange way of connecting\nwith people. But to be honest, I don't mind it.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_028: I am interested in hearing more. Now, I would hear\na song that you enjoy playing.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_029: A song I enjoy playing? An unexpected request\ncoming from you. But fine. I'll play for you.
MID_SE_Dit_Led_A_030: Now sit quietly and listen. And if you draw your\nsword on me again...I will kill you.